# Caddy configuration (slide 132).
# {$DOMAIN} is filled in from the container's DOMAIN environment variable.
#
# Giving Caddy a domain name is all it takes to switch on HTTPS and the
# redirect from HTTP. On the slides the certificate comes from a public
# certificate authority, which needs a server reachable from the internet.
# "tls internal" makes Caddy act as its own certificate authority instead.
{$DOMAIN} {
	tls internal
	root * /srv
	file_server
}
